# The Mackey-Glass equation
# Blood cells are made at a rate that depends on how many there were a time
# tau ago. A long enough delay turns the steady count into irregular
# swings (Mackey and Glass, 1977).
x'=beta*delay(x,tau)/(1+delay(x,tau)^n)-gamma*x
par beta=0.2,gamma=0.1,n=10,tau=17
init x=1.2
x(0)=1.2
@ total=600,dt=0.05,meth=rungekutta,delay=20,maxstor=20000
@ xp=t,yp=x,xlo=0,xhi=600,ylo=0,yhi=1.6
done
